# Pramniaga Code Standards

Before editing, follow [`.cursor/CODE_STANDARDS.md`](../CODE_STANDARDS.md) and [`.cursor/FILE_STRUCTURE.md`](../FILE_STRUCTURE.md).

- File header on every hand-written module: `Purpose`, `Exports` (if useful), `Last updated`, `Author: Pramniaga`.
- Every public export: named docs — TS `Name - …` + `@param` / `@returns`; Python `name - …` + Args / Returns.
- Names must be intent-first (`defaultCompany`, `can_browse_stock`); no opaque `tmp`/`data2`.
- CSS: prefer design tokens; custom classes are domain+role (`login-brand-mesh`); style constants end in `Class`.
- UI labels must match metric meaning (draft vs total).
- Never let client `payload` override `doctype`/`name` on create; require company scoping for stock queries.
- Split at ~300 lines or a 4th unrelated concern via facade package (template: `api/inventory/`).
- Frontend placement: `components/ui` (barrel), `layout`, `components/<domain>`, `pages/<domain>`, `lib`.
- Preserve `pramniaga.api.<domain>.<fn>` paths. Do not drive-by reformat unrelated files.
